WEBVTT

00:01.467 --> 00:04.478
♪ it seems today that all you see ♪

00:04.546 --> 00:08.097
♪ is violence in movies and sex on tv ♪

00:08.165 --> 00:11.646
♪ but where are those good ol
d-fashioned values ♪

00:11.714 --> 00:14.692
♪ on which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.761 --> 00:18.479
♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.547 --> 00:21.526
♪ lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.594 --> 00:23.134
♪ all the things that make us ♪

00:23.201 --> 00:24.506
♪ laugh and cry ♪

00:24.573 --> 00:27.151
♪ he's... A... Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.128 --> 00:38.170
Good evening. I'm diane simmons.

00:38.238 --> 00:41.418
In traffic news, heavy gridlock
on the 195 interchange.

00:41.486 --> 00:44.699
We now go live to drunk billy
in the channel 5 newscopter.

00:48.352 --> 00:49.588
This just in.

00:49.656 --> 00:52.468
Channel 5 newscopter pilot
drunk billy passed away today.

00:52.536 --> 00:54.143
In anticipation of this event,

00:54.212 --> 00:55.549
We put together a clip package

00:55.616 --> 00:58.093
Featuring some of billy's
work for channel 5 news.

01:12.395 --> 01:15.239
"I'm still hungry,
" said the very hungry caterpillar.

01:15.308 --> 01:17.183
"but you've already..."

01:20.867 --> 01:23.044
Drunk billy will be missed.

01:23.111 --> 01:25.086
But what you shouldn't
miss is the quahog rodeo,

01:25.154 --> 01:26.696
Coming to the civic center this Friday.

01:26.763 --> 01:28.334
Tickets are on sale now.

01:28.401 --> 01:29.976
And for those of you who
are handy with a horse,

01:30.044 --> 01:31.719
Entry spots are still open.

01:31.786 --> 01:33.561
Oh, god, this seems like
the kind of thing peter...

01:33.629 --> 01:34.865
Too late, brian.

01:34.933 --> 01:36.473
Peter, you're gonna enter the rodeo?

01:36.540 --> 01:37.678
That's stupid.

01:37.746 --> 01:38.885
You don't know anything about horses,

01:38.953 --> 01:40.456
And you're in terrible shape.

01:40.525 --> 01:42.367
You know, that's the difference
between you and me, lois.

01:42.435 --> 01:43.741
When life comes knocking at the door,

01:43.809 --> 01:45.079
You go and hide in the kitchen.

01:45.147 --> 01:46.889
I fling the door wide open and I say,

01:46.956 --> 01:48.327
"peter griffin here. What do you got?"

01:48.395 --> 01:49.935
And if that don't convince you,
look at this.

01:50.003 --> 01:51.377
<i>In this week's tv guide, it says,</i>

01:51.445 --> 01:53.015
"peter gets more than he bargained for

01:53.083 --> 01:54.256
When he joins the rodeo."

01:54.324 --> 01:55.560
<i>Well, it's in the guide.</i>

01:55.627 --> 01:57.203
Hey, can we make that a thing?

01:57.270 --> 01:59.045
<i>Can we start calling tv guide, "the
guide"?</i>

01:59.113 --> 02:00.517
You know what? I'm not even asking anymore.

02:00.585 --> 02:01.723
That's what we're doing.

02:01.791 --> 02:03.869
Who says I couldn't be a rodeo star?

02:03.936 --> 02:06.982
I got more cowboy blood
in me than billy the kid.

02:07.050 --> 02:12.774
♪ well, he robbed his way
from utah to oklahoma ♪

02:12.842 --> 02:17.329
♪ and the law just could not
seem to track him down ♪

02:19.373 --> 02:22.386
♪ and it served his legend well ♪

02:22.454 --> 02:24.865
♪ for the folks, they loved to tell ♪

02:24.932 --> 02:29.485
♪ about when billy the kid came to town. ♪

02:47.772 --> 02:49.646
♪ ♪

03:13.557 --> 03:14.796
Hyah!

03:23.402 --> 03:25.077
Dad, what are you doing?!

03:25.146 --> 03:26.281
All right, meg, this is only gonna hurt

03:26.349 --> 03:27.421
For about three weeks.

03:28.593 --> 03:30.066
What the hell?

03:30.135 --> 03:32.645
That there's my steer, griffin.

03:38.071 --> 03:39.846
All right, lois. Go ahead. Say it.

03:41.052 --> 03:44.869
Chris, it's time for supper.

03:44.937 --> 03:46.342
Ho der, ho der, ho der!

03:46.409 --> 03:48.017
Ho der, ho der, ho der, ho der!

03:48.085 --> 03:50.328
Ho der, ho der, ho der! Ho der, ho der!

03:50.396 --> 03:52.301
Ho der, ho der, ho der.

03:52.373 --> 03:55.017
ho der, ho der, ho der.

03:55.084 --> 03:56.890
Ho der.

03:56.958 --> 03:59.769
All right. I am ready for the rodeo.

04:03.288 --> 04:05.633
Mom, when's it dad's turn?

04:05.701 --> 04:06.869
I don't know, chris.

04:06.937 --> 04:08.679
But I think we should
all pray for your father

04:08.747 --> 04:10.320
That he comes out of this uninjured.

04:10.388 --> 04:11.859
Those horses stink.

04:11.928 --> 04:13.401
And it's too hot in here.

04:13.469 --> 04:16.481
I fell asleep in the car, so now I'm cranky.

04:16.549 --> 04:18.557
This is a disgusting display.

04:18.626 --> 04:19.863
Boy, you can say that again.

04:19.930 --> 04:22.979
Nothing like a bunch of adult
men teasing animals for fun.

04:23.046 --> 04:24.886
It's amazing that this is still legal.

04:24.953 --> 04:26.194
The only reason I'm here

04:26.262 --> 04:28.304
Is 'cause my idiot friend is in the rodeo.

04:28.372 --> 04:30.481
I only came 'cause I'm
writing a magazine article.

04:30.549 --> 04:31.852
One of the competitors

04:31.920 --> 04:34.095
Is a 13-year-old female riding prodigy.

04:34.163 --> 04:35.906
Apparently she got on the bull to miscarry,

04:35.974 --> 04:38.049
And found out she had a talent for it.

04:38.116 --> 04:41.464
Announcer : Ladies and gentlemen,
give an indifferent east coast welcome

04:41.532 --> 04:44.344
To the newest bullrider, peter the kid!

04:49.904 --> 04:51.913
You know what I am back at the ranch?

04:51.980 --> 04:53.821
I'm a breeding bull.

04:53.889 --> 04:55.431
W-what-what's that?

04:55.499 --> 04:57.572
You gonna find out.

04:57.639 --> 04:58.679
Where you goin', fatty?

04:58.746 --> 04:59.882
We gonna have a party.

05:01.158 --> 05:02.393
No! No!

05:07.886 --> 05:09.193
No! No!

05:11.137 --> 05:12.942
So, what magazine do you write for?

05:13.010 --> 05:14.450
<i>I'm the editor for teen people.</i>

05:14.517 --> 05:15.824
Editor?

05:15.892 --> 05:18.503
Well, gosh, you know,
I'm something of a writer myself.

05:18.570 --> 05:20.648
<i>I-I wrote for the new yorker
for a little while.</i>

05:20.716 --> 05:22.118
Wow, that's impressive.

05:22.187 --> 05:23.226
Are you looking for work?

05:23.294 --> 05:24.630
Oh, no. No, no, no.

05:24.699 --> 05:26.474
I-I never have to look too far for that.

05:26.542 --> 05:27.509
I... W-w-what are you...

05:27.578 --> 05:29.052
What do you... What-what do you got?

05:29.120 --> 05:30.894
Well, we're looking for
someone to write a piece

05:30.962 --> 05:32.132
On the everyday activities

05:32.200 --> 05:33.942
Of the average american teenage girl.

05:34.009 --> 05:35.952
Oh, I love teenage girls.

05:36.019 --> 05:37.356
It's all ahead of them, you know?

05:37.424 --> 05:38.865
They haven't turned into bitches yet.

05:38.933 --> 05:40.604
Oh, it's true.

05:40.671 --> 05:42.312
What happened to all of us?

05:42.381 --> 05:45.125
I got a house on the cape.
Maybe you come visit.

05:45.193 --> 05:46.634
Maybe.

05:46.701 --> 05:48.577
Maybe you call a few days in advance

05:48.645 --> 05:50.048
To give me time to get the house clean.

05:50.116 --> 05:51.189
Okay.

05:51.256 --> 05:52.426
Maybe you bring a blazer,

05:52.494 --> 05:54.537
So we can go to a wider
range of restaurants.

05:54.605 --> 05:55.941
I'll-I'll bring a blazer.

05:59.260 --> 06:00.496
You see this, rupert?

06:00.565 --> 06:02.405
Most children build a sand castle.

06:02.473 --> 06:05.888
But I'm building a sand retreat
for singles in their 30s.

06:05.955 --> 06:07.663
: Hi, I'm jeremy.

06:07.731 --> 06:09.573
I work in corporate finance.

06:09.642 --> 06:12.119
: Hi, I'm a french canadian girl

06:12.186 --> 06:13.893
Down here on my vacation.

06:13.961 --> 06:17.041
It's a big deal for me to
be down here on my own.

06:17.108 --> 06:19.486
I like the swimming pool with a bar in it

06:19.554 --> 06:22.433
'cause you can sit on a barstool
and you're in the water.

06:22.500 --> 06:25.044
: I like how all the food
and drink is included

06:25.112 --> 06:26.518
In the price of the ticket.

06:26.586 --> 06:28.091
: Yeah, that way you don't have

06:28.159 --> 06:30.435
To bring your cash down from the room.

06:30.503 --> 06:32.712
: Okay, I was just looking
for a friend of mine,

06:32.780 --> 06:34.422
So maybe I'll see you later.

06:34.491 --> 06:36.061
: Good for you, janine.

06:36.129 --> 06:39.579
You promised yourself you'd
talk to somebody and you did it.

06:39.647 --> 06:41.352
: Brian, what are you doing up there?

06:41.424 --> 06:42.358
Shh. I'm writing an article

06:42.427 --> 06:44.436
On teenage girls for a magazine.

06:44.503 --> 06:46.546
I'm studying meg to see
what goes on during her day.

06:46.613 --> 06:48.385
Well, be careful you don't
fall off that ladder.

06:48.454 --> 06:50.161
Not all dogs go to heaven.

06:50.229 --> 06:51.836
So, says here you were involved

06:51.903 --> 06:53.577
In the plotting of September 11?

06:53.644 --> 06:56.893
Well, that's what they get
for supporting israel.

06:56.961 --> 06:59.773
Hyuck, yuck, yuck. Gawsh.

06:59.841 --> 07:02.352
Okay, into the eternal pit of fire you go.

07:02.419 --> 07:05.165
Wa-hoo-hoo-hoo-ee!

07:10.522 --> 07:12.767
You know, brian, just because
you're writing a profile

07:12.834 --> 07:14.441
On teenage girls, it doesn't mean you have

07:14.509 --> 07:17.756
To be a creepy stalker and
follow meg around all day.

07:17.824 --> 07:19.027
It's called research, stewie.

07:19.095 --> 07:20.000
I'm just being thorough.

07:20.068 --> 07:21.876
Where the hell is she going?

07:21.944 --> 07:23.180
There's nothing out in this part of town.

07:27.067 --> 07:28.204
What is that, brian?

07:28.272 --> 07:30.180
What is an adult correctional institute?

07:30.248 --> 07:31.285
It's a prison, stewie.

07:31.353 --> 07:32.492
Ah.

07:32.559 --> 07:34.197
One would think they could just say that.

07:38.452 --> 07:39.725
Hi, meg.

07:39.793 --> 07:40.962
Hi, luke.

07:50.509 --> 07:51.746
Oh, my god.

07:51.813 --> 07:53.922
Meg's dating a convict!

07:53.990 --> 07:56.300
Oh looks like consuela's son is in prison.

07:56.368 --> 07:58.879
I see you soon, rodrigo.

07:58.946 --> 08:00.789
<i>Si, mama.</i>

08:08.443 --> 08:10.149
It's really good to see you, meg.

08:10.218 --> 08:11.388
It's been a while.

08:11.456 --> 08:13.063
I know. I'm sorry, luke.

08:13.131 --> 08:14.502
It's just so hard to get over here

08:14.570 --> 08:16.043
Without anybody finding out.

08:16.111 --> 08:17.987
Have you gotten all the letters
and hair that I've sent?

08:18.055 --> 08:19.224
It's the only thing

08:19.292 --> 08:20.800
That's getting me by, meg. Thank you.

08:20.868 --> 08:22.307
How'd your parole hearing go?

08:22.375 --> 08:23.712
Not good.

08:23.780 --> 08:25.622
Looks like I'm gonna be in
here another three years.

08:25.690 --> 08:27.094
Oh, luke.

08:27.162 --> 08:28.969
Oh, I don't expect you to wait for me, meg.

08:29.037 --> 08:30.077
No, I will, luke.

08:30.144 --> 08:31.648
If it takes ten years or 20 years,

08:31.716 --> 08:33.357
I will be here when you get out.

08:43.104 --> 08:44.642
Oh, my god!

08:44.710 --> 08:46.284
Meg's involved with a convict!

08:46.351 --> 08:48.327
Wow, meg's like one of those crazy chicks

08:48.395 --> 08:50.537
Who hooks up with an even crazier guy.

08:55.695 --> 08:57.066
Brian, you bastard!

08:57.135 --> 08:58.541
How could you do this to me?!

08:58.609 --> 09:00.350
I'm sorry, meg. I had to tell them!

09:00.418 --> 09:01.988
Don't give him crap for this, meg.

09:02.057 --> 09:04.166
He did exactly the right
thing by coming to us.

09:04.235 --> 09:06.244
Don't you know what kind of fire

09:06.311 --> 09:07.719
You're playing with, dating a prisoner?

09:07.787 --> 09:09.759
Hold on, lois. This is
some serious parenting.

09:09.827 --> 09:12.304
I'm gonna go put on my cosby sweater.

09:12.372 --> 09:14.080
Mom, you don't understand!

09:14.147 --> 09:16.791
Luke and I really connect, very deeply!

09:16.860 --> 09:19.772
He's all alone in there,
and I'm all alone out here.

09:19.841 --> 09:21.814
In a way, we're both in prison.

09:21.883 --> 09:23.824
Well, meg, there's a big difference there.

09:23.893 --> 09:25.196
He's in prison for a reason.

09:25.264 --> 09:26.538
He broke the law!

09:26.606 --> 09:28.146
He robbed a convenience store

09:28.213 --> 09:30.386
To pay for medication for his mom.

09:30.458 --> 09:33.537
Oh, I'm sure he gave you a
very convincing sob story.

09:33.605 --> 09:36.049
It's not a sob story! It's true!

09:36.118 --> 09:37.655
Frankly, I don't care, meg.

09:37.722 --> 09:39.530
I do not want you seeing him again!

09:39.598 --> 09:40.671
I can't find the sweater.

09:40.738 --> 09:42.143
How the hell did you even meet him?!

09:42.211 --> 09:43.818
We had a pen pal project at school,

09:43.886 --> 09:45.057
And when it was over,

09:45.124 --> 09:46.998
Luke and I just kind of
kept writing to each other.

09:47.066 --> 09:48.273
Well, it stops now!

09:48.341 --> 09:50.113
But, mom, I love him!

09:50.181 --> 09:51.688
It stops now, meg!

09:51.755 --> 09:53.529
Your mother's right, meg.
You got to be careful

09:53.597 --> 09:55.068
Who you get involved with romantically.

09:56.311 --> 09:57.480
Hello?

09:57.548 --> 09:58.619
I'm in the mood for some coitus.

09:58.688 --> 10:00.092
Get over here.

10:00.160 --> 10:01.333
I can't. I'm with my family.

10:01.401 --> 10:03.476
Pick up wine on the way.

10:03.544 --> 10:05.854
Well, angela, if I'm
really the only guy at work

10:05.922 --> 10:08.433
Who can solve it, I'll be right there.

10:16.572 --> 10:18.780
Luke!

10:18.848 --> 10:20.151
What are you doing here?!

10:20.219 --> 10:21.527
I escaped, meg.

10:21.595 --> 10:22.931
I escaped 'cause I just couldn't bear

10:22.999 --> 10:24.272
Another second away from you.

10:24.340 --> 10:26.348
My god, how did you get out?

10:26.416 --> 10:28.322
I filed down a toothbrush to a fine point

10:28.390 --> 10:29.964
And stabbed the guard with the most kids.

10:30.032 --> 10:31.674
What?! I'm just kidding.

10:31.742 --> 10:34.821
Oh. I'm still getting used
to your sense of humor.

10:34.888 --> 10:36.964
Actually, there was a
riot in the prison yard,

10:37.033 --> 10:38.236
And I slipped over the fence.

10:38.304 --> 10:40.178
Well, well, quick, get in
here before somebody sees you!

10:45.402 --> 10:48.282
Oh, meg, I've wanted to do that for so long.

10:48.350 --> 10:50.794
And it's nice to be in front
of someone for a change.

10:52.203 --> 10:54.713
Now I know that was a joke!

10:54.781 --> 10:55.984
whatever.

10:56.052 --> 10:57.392
Hey, meg?

10:57.459 --> 10:59.067
Can I talk to you for a second?

11:00.908 --> 11:03.957
Uh, yeah, come on in.

11:04.024 --> 11:07.907
Listen, uh, I feel like
I should explain myself

11:07.975 --> 11:09.181
A little bit here.

11:09.249 --> 11:11.525
I'm sorry I had to tell
lois what was going on.

11:11.593 --> 11:13.097
You just, you gotta realize

11:13.164 --> 11:14.740
I was only thinking about your safety and...

11:19.597 --> 11:21.706
Luke, you might as well come out now.

11:23.111 --> 11:25.155
Luke! What the...
? They let you out of jail?!

11:25.221 --> 11:26.862
Not exactly.

11:26.930 --> 11:29.743
He broke out to see me, brian.
We're in love.

11:29.811 --> 11:31.148
Meg, are you crazy?!

11:31.216 --> 11:32.823
You can't harbor a fugitive.
That's a felony.

11:32.890 --> 11:33.893
Only if someone finds out.

11:33.961 --> 11:35.301
Are you gonna do it?

11:35.369 --> 11:36.776
Are you gonna tell on me again?

11:36.844 --> 11:37.979
Well, I, I...

11:38.047 --> 11:40.225
Brian, will you call me
on my mickey mouse phone?

11:40.292 --> 11:41.328
Wait a second.

11:41.396 --> 11:43.371
Why is that guy wearing a prison jumpsuit?

11:43.439 --> 11:44.377
Think, peter, think.

11:44.445 --> 11:46.756
Wait. Hang on.

11:46.824 --> 11:48.428
Sunday, Sunday... Here it is.

11:48.495 --> 11:50.170
"peter gets more than he bargains for

11:50.238 --> 11:52.682
When he joins the rodeo." boy, did I.

11:52.751 --> 11:54.691
"and meg dates a prison escapee"!

11:54.760 --> 11:56.731
Oh, no! Luke, run!

11:59.850 --> 12:01.287
Joe, it's peter! Two things:

12:01.356 --> 12:04.000
First of all, when I was over
at your house the other day,

12:04.068 --> 12:06.345
I forgot to tell you how
much I like the rearrangement

12:06.412 --> 12:08.187
You and bonnie did with
your living room furniture.

12:08.255 --> 12:09.728
Second of all, come outside!

12:09.795 --> 12:11.536
There's an escaped convict
running across the street!

12:26.271 --> 12:28.313
No, luke, don't run downhill!

12:35.983 --> 12:38.293
You're going to jail, punk!

12:42.010 --> 12:44.052
No, mr. Swanson, you can't take him!

12:44.120 --> 12:45.461
Yes, I can, meg.

12:45.529 --> 12:47.066
He's going back to jail.

12:47.133 --> 12:48.474
Well, if you're taking him to jail,

12:48.542 --> 12:49.815
You have to take me, too!

12:49.882 --> 12:51.152
I know. That's the plan.

12:51.220 --> 12:54.401
You're under arrest for
harboring an escaped convict.

12:54.469 --> 12:56.410
Oh, well, that's only
fair because after all,

12:56.478 --> 12:57.986
I did hide him from the...

12:58.054 --> 12:59.021
<i>What?!</i>

13:07.498 --> 13:08.634
Uh, hi.

13:08.701 --> 13:11.982
Did you also get caught
trying to vote in ohio?

13:16.772 --> 13:18.045
Well, this is it.

13:18.112 --> 13:19.518
Meg gets out of jail today.

13:19.586 --> 13:21.827
Already? It seems like just
yesterday we rented her room

13:21.895 --> 13:24.808
To that fly that wants to leave,
but can't figure it out.

13:26.484 --> 13:27.519
Okay, now where now?

13:27.591 --> 13:28.560
Right there.

13:28.629 --> 13:29.998
I'm having some trouble here.

13:30.065 --> 13:31.841
It's right there!
It's right in front of you!

13:31.909 --> 13:33.984
Okay, I can hear you.
Volume's not a problem.

13:34.052 --> 13:35.929
I'm just not quite seeing
what you're referring to.

13:35.996 --> 13:37.400
Okay, then fly, fly out the window.

13:37.467 --> 13:39.242
Up here maybe? No, to your left!

13:39.310 --> 13:40.985
No, that's not it. That's just more wall.

13:41.053 --> 13:42.894
How many eyes do you have, huh?!

13:42.962 --> 13:45.439
Just two, same number as you,
but I can't, I'm not...

13:45.506 --> 13:46.877
Just go! Oh, my god!

13:46.945 --> 13:48.353
Whatever it is you're driving at,

13:48.421 --> 13:49.622
I'm just apparently not getting it...

13:49.691 --> 13:50.864
You're right there!

13:50.933 --> 13:52.370
...So I'm just gonna go back upstairs.

13:52.437 --> 13:55.015
I think we should all go
together to pick meg up.

13:55.082 --> 13:57.427
She's probably a little fragile
after being in there so long,

13:57.495 --> 14:00.072
And I'm sure she'll be
heartened to see our faces.

14:01.847 --> 14:04.158
I'm home. You're all my bitches now.

14:05.834 --> 14:06.870
Okay.

14:10.688 --> 14:12.896
Meg! You look so different.

14:12.964 --> 14:13.935
How was prison?

14:14.003 --> 14:15.374
First question:

14:15.442 --> 14:17.752
Who's the biggest,
toughest guy in this house?

14:17.820 --> 14:19.728
Well, I don't like to toot my own horn,

14:19.796 --> 14:21.371
But I believe I hold the distinction...

14:30.178 --> 14:31.986
My house now, bitch!

14:32.054 --> 14:33.527
Now who's the funniest?

14:33.595 --> 14:35.199
I know my way around a joke.

14:37.177 --> 14:38.583
For god's sake, dad,

14:38.651 --> 14:41.029
Have some humility! It'll save your life!

14:41.097 --> 14:45.145
There better be beer in the fridge.

14:45.214 --> 14:47.992
Boy, I liked her better when
she was more predictable...

14:48.060 --> 14:50.505
Like the stock photos
on a corporate website.

14:50.573 --> 14:52.748
I'm a woman in a lab coat wearing goggles,

14:52.816 --> 14:55.159
Staring intently at a beaker
that I'm holding near my face.

14:55.227 --> 14:56.835
I'm a latino in a hardhat,

14:56.903 --> 14:59.581
But I'm also wearing a tie
so you know I'm a supervisor.

14:59.649 --> 15:01.691
We're college students
listening to our professor,

15:01.759 --> 15:04.938
<i>But the class is taking
place outside?!</i>

15:12.040 --> 15:13.343
Hey.

15:13.411 --> 15:15.721
Meg! What the hell are you doing in here?!

15:15.789 --> 15:17.798
Shower time. Yeah, for me.

15:17.865 --> 15:19.975
Not-not for... What are you
doing with that loofah?

15:20.042 --> 15:20.945
Don't worry about it.

15:23.056 --> 15:25.064
You told me not to worry about it!

15:25.132 --> 15:27.577
I shoulda been worried the whole time!

15:29.789 --> 15:32.968
Meg, honey? I did all your laundry.

15:33.036 --> 15:35.982
Oh, my god, what is that smell?

15:36.050 --> 15:37.156
It's my poop bucket.

15:37.223 --> 15:38.393
What the hell?!

15:38.461 --> 15:40.737
I'm used to going to the
bathroom in my room.

15:40.806 --> 15:42.312
That's disgusting!

15:42.381 --> 15:44.790
No, you use the toilet
here like everyone else!

15:44.859 --> 15:46.567
No. Ugh!

15:46.634 --> 15:48.038
God, it smells horrible!

15:48.106 --> 15:50.784
Well, can you at least empty
it each time you use it?

15:50.852 --> 15:52.392
I like to fill it up.

15:52.461 --> 15:53.797
I'm not making a million trips.

15:53.865 --> 15:57.182
Oh, my god, are you using
my shirts as toilet paper?

15:57.250 --> 15:58.353
Yeah. And I think

15:58.420 --> 16:00.730
I might need some right now.

16:00.797 --> 16:03.677
Get out now or stay and get weird.

16:03.745 --> 16:05.219
Your call, warden.

16:09.841 --> 16:11.580
Hey, who's the new dude?

16:11.651 --> 16:13.222
Oh, my god, that's meg griffin!

16:13.289 --> 16:15.465
She just got out of prison!

16:15.533 --> 16:17.711
Hey, meg, what'd they put you in jail for,

16:17.778 --> 16:18.814
Being ugly?

16:20.624 --> 16:22.063
Hey, meg, what happened?

16:22.131 --> 16:23.904
Did you get out early for fat behavior?

16:25.713 --> 16:26.920
Nice tattoo.

16:26.988 --> 16:28.693
Did you get your butt hair braided, too,

16:28.762 --> 16:30.502
While you were in there?

16:30.569 --> 16:32.746
What'd you do, carve a gun out of soap

16:32.815 --> 16:35.492
And then not wash with it? Ha-ha! P.U.

16:37.234 --> 16:39.779
Hey, meg, are you gonna take those soda cans

16:39.847 --> 16:41.753
To the shawskank redemption center?

16:56.121 --> 16:58.432
Peter, meg's been suspended from school.

16:58.498 --> 17:00.175
That's okay. Whatever she wants to do.

17:00.242 --> 17:02.150
She cracked three kids' skulls open!

17:02.218 --> 17:04.024
Ever since she's gotten out of prison,

17:04.092 --> 17:05.833
She is completely out of control.

17:05.900 --> 17:07.308
Don't you see?

17:07.375 --> 17:09.315
That's what the penal
system does in this country.

17:09.382 --> 17:10.857
It turns small-time offenders
into hardened criminals.

17:10.924 --> 17:13.235
Look at meg. They took
an innocent little girl

17:13.302 --> 17:15.645
And turned her into a psychotic,
sociopathic freak.

17:17.522 --> 17:18.792
What'd you say, brian?

17:18.860 --> 17:21.304
Oh, I-I was just picking
up on something lois said.

17:21.372 --> 17:22.880
What-what was it? What'd you say, lois?

17:22.948 --> 17:24.318
Something about meg being a freak?

17:24.386 --> 17:26.495
Oh, no, I didn't say anything.

17:26.562 --> 17:28.170
Uh, peter said something about meg,

17:28.238 --> 17:29.946
Which I completely disagree with.

17:30.013 --> 17:31.283
That-that-that wasn't me.

17:31.352 --> 17:32.993
Stewie was really laying
into meg about something.

17:33.061 --> 17:33.896
Yeah, it was stewie.

17:33.964 --> 17:35.036
Definitely stewie.

17:35.104 --> 17:36.842
Oh, so now everyone understands me.

17:36.911 --> 17:39.387
Look, meg, we're just worried about you.

17:39.456 --> 17:41.531
Well, don't. I can take care of myself.

17:41.599 --> 17:43.608
I'll be outta here by the end of the week.

17:43.676 --> 17:45.517
Punch yourself in the face.

17:46.622 --> 17:47.862
Punch yourself in the face!

17:49.200 --> 17:51.010
All right, he doesn't know what he's doing.

17:51.078 --> 17:54.023
You, fatso, punch your baby in the fa...

17:54.091 --> 17:55.263
I did good, meg?

17:55.330 --> 17:57.171
Shut up.

17:57.238 --> 18:00.220
I did good. I did good.

18:08.726 --> 18:09.929
Drive.

18:09.997 --> 18:12.541
Uh, any particular direction?

18:12.609 --> 18:13.614
That way.

18:16.127 --> 18:17.697
You're gonna help me get some money

18:17.769 --> 18:19.407
So I can get out of this town.

18:19.474 --> 18:20.881
Really? Where are you gonna go?

18:20.950 --> 18:23.058
I don't know. Somewhere far away.

18:23.126 --> 18:24.966
Maybe china.

18:25.034 --> 18:26.674
I hear they got nascar there now.

18:34.578 --> 18:37.858
What kind of birdhouse can
you build with popsicles,

18:37.930 --> 18:39.299
Roofies, and a mallet?

18:39.367 --> 18:43.019
It's for a rare african bird called "
nunya business."

18:45.631 --> 18:47.336
Hi, meg. Can I help you?

18:47.405 --> 18:49.446
Hands in the air, goldman!

18:49.514 --> 18:51.624
Oh, my god, what are you doing?!

18:51.692 --> 18:52.628
Gimme your money!

18:52.696 --> 18:54.436
Here, here, just take this jar

18:54.503 --> 18:55.677
For the leukemia kids.

18:55.745 --> 18:57.282
I don't give it to 'em anyhow.

18:57.350 --> 18:58.657
Meg, put down the gun.

18:58.725 --> 19:00.329
Brian, get back in the car!

19:00.397 --> 19:03.848
Look, don't do this. This isn't you, meg.

19:03.915 --> 19:05.758
What happened to the girl we used to know?

19:05.825 --> 19:07.698
The one that luke fell in love with?

19:07.766 --> 19:09.072
The one he's expecting to see

19:09.140 --> 19:11.282
When he steps out of
that prison in 40 years?

19:11.350 --> 19:12.686
I don't care about luke.

19:12.755 --> 19:15.131
I don't need him. I don't need anyone!

19:15.200 --> 19:16.808
Look, if you don't put the gun down,

19:16.875 --> 19:18.450
I'm gonna be forced to call the police.

19:18.517 --> 19:19.954
Good! Call the police!

19:20.022 --> 19:21.095
I want you to!

19:21.162 --> 19:23.268
What do I care if I go back to prison?

19:23.336 --> 19:24.610
Nobody cares about me anyway!

19:24.678 --> 19:26.385
You're wrong, meg.

19:26.453 --> 19:28.125
I wanna show you something.

19:30.505 --> 19:32.982
<i>Teen people?</i>

19:33.049 --> 19:34.823
It's the article I wrote about you.

19:34.891 --> 19:37.235
You wrote an article about me?

19:37.303 --> 19:38.305
They wanted a story

19:38.373 --> 19:40.081
About a typical teenage girl.

19:40.149 --> 19:43.832
Is it "a fistful of backne:
Tale of a teenage loser"?

19:43.900 --> 19:46.212
Yeah, they make the title.
Read paragraph three.

19:46.279 --> 19:47.984
This isn't a library, you know.

19:48.052 --> 19:50.495
"and in the face of every
adolescent challenge,

19:50.563 --> 19:52.807
"she looks at the world through hopeful eyes

19:52.874 --> 19:54.850
"and maintains an uncommon resilience

19:54.918 --> 19:56.391
"that can only be admired.

19:56.459 --> 20:00.073
"in this sense, meg griffin is
not the typical american girl.

20:00.141 --> 20:03.422
She is far sweeter and kinder than that."

20:03.490 --> 20:06.471
Oh, god, that is so nice, brian.

20:06.539 --> 20:07.910
Did you mean all that?

20:07.978 --> 20:09.384
Of course I did.

20:09.453 --> 20:12.164
Oh, my god, I-I can't believe I did this.

20:12.231 --> 20:15.511
I was just so tired of being
everyone's whipping girl

20:15.579 --> 20:17.989
That it felt kind of good
to do some of the whipping.

20:18.057 --> 20:19.733
Give me the gun, meg.

20:22.546 --> 20:25.090
Thanks for reminding me who I really am.

20:30.749 --> 20:32.492
Well, at least I didn't get robbed.

20:34.001 --> 20:37.448
And what can I do for you four
fine black gentlemen today?

20:41.636 --> 20:44.615
I got to say, meg, I like you
so much better like this.

20:44.683 --> 20:46.053
Me, too, meg.

20:46.121 --> 20:47.896
God, it must have been horrible in there.

20:47.964 --> 20:49.303
It wasn't so bad.

20:49.371 --> 20:51.043
I met wesley snipes. Is that right?

20:51.111 --> 20:53.152
Yeah. Oh, and you know what's funny?

20:53.221 --> 20:54.930
<i>He was inmate 57, too.</i>

20:54.998 --> 20:55.798
Huh?

20:55.866 --> 20:57.809
He was inmate 57?

20:57.877 --> 21:00.321
<i>See, he did a movie called
passenger 57.</i>

21:00.389 --> 21:01.457
Ah.

21:01.525 --> 21:02.933
Well, terrific.

21:03.000 --> 21:05.209
Always end on a strong joke.

21:05.210 --> 22:06.210
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru